Escape split_awvalid_drop: pre-release bug, M-port AWVALID drops before AWREADY
and the write is lost. In the drop that had the bug, the splitter drove
O_M_AWVALID straight to the pins as w_m_awch_en & I_M_WREADY with no AWREADY
hold term. The fix added register slices on the splitter's M-port AW and W,
and the later 1xN switch adds a skid buffer on the pin AW. This takes out both
AW slices, so the pin AWVALID is the splitter's again: on a split burst the
next sub-burst's W beats enter the W slice ahead of its AW, the beat counter
moves, and AWVALID falls without AWREADY, dropping that sub-burst's AW. The
splitter W slice stays: without it the switch's WREADY (which waits for
AWVALID) and the splitter's AWVALID (which waits for WREADY) form a loop that
never raises either.
Applied to a build-time copy of RTL/ by make build ESCAPE=split_awvalid_drop.

--- a/RTL/AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_SS.v
+++ b/RTL/AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_SS.v
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
     parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_RCH_RS_EN  = 1,
     parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_AWCH_RS_EN = 1,
     parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_WCH_RS_EN  = 1,
-    parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_M_AWCH_RS_EN = 1,
+    parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_M_AWCH_RS_EN = 0,
     parameter   AOU_AXIMUX_1XN_M_WCH_RS_EN = 1,
 
     parameter   SN            = 4,
--- a/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR.v
+++ b/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR.v
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
     parameter   WR_MO_CNT = 64,
     parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_SLV_ARCH_RS_EN = 1,
     parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_SLV_RCH_RS_EN = 1,
-    parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_MST_AWCH_RS_EN = 1,
+    parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_MST_AWCH_RS_EN = 0,
     parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_MST_WCH_RS_EN = 1,
     parameter   AOU_AXI_SPLIT_TR_MST_BCH_RS_EN = 0,
